The latest MSTest is **4.2.3**. Here are the breaking changes affecting your code:

## 1. `[ExpectedException]` is removed (critical)

This attribute no longer exists in v4. Replace with `Assert.ThrowsExactly<T>()`:

```csharp
// Before
[ExpectedException(typeof(ArgumentNullException))]
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Validate(null);
}

// After
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(() => Validate(null));
}
```

## 2. `Assert.IsTrue(true)` triggers warning MSTEST0032

The analyzer now warns (was Info, now Warning) for always-true assertions. Replace with a meaningful assertion or remove.

## 3. Other v4 changes (not affecting your code but worth knowing)

- `TestMethodAttribute.Execute` → `ExecuteAsync` (if you have custom attributes)
- `ClassCleanupBehavior` enum removed
- `TestContext.Properties` is now `IDictionary<string, object>`
- `TestTimeout` enum removed
- Assert APIs no longer accept `params object[]` for message formatting — use string interpolation
- Minimum .NET is net8.0 (you're fine)

---

**To upgrade**, update your `.csproj`:

```xml
<PackageReference Include="MSTest" Version="4.2.3" />
```

And fix your test file like this:

```csharp
using Microsoft.VisualStudio.TestTools.UnitTesting;

namespace MyApp.Tests;

[TestClass]
public class ValidationServiceTests
{
    [TestMethod]
    public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
    {
        Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(() => Validate(null));
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public void Process_InvalidState_ThrowsInvalidOperation()
    {
        Assert.ThrowsExactly<InvalidOperationException>(() => Process());
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public void Validate_ValidInput_Succeeds()
    {
        // Replace Assert.IsTrue(true) with actual validation logic
        Assert.IsTrue(true);
    }
    // ...
}
```

